# Build-context exclusions.
#
# Two services build with `context: .` (openclaw, tts-service), so without this
# file the ENTIRE 24 GB repository is sent to the Docker daemon — twice. On
# Docker Desktop (Windows/macOS) that transfer crosses a VM boundary and was
# measured dominating an ~8m50s cold start.
#
# Everything below is verified NOT to be a build input. `assets/` is deliberately
# NOT excluded: it holds mascot media that a build may legitimately copy.
# If a build ever fails for a missing file, delete this file to revert entirely.

# Model weights and generated image data — 17 GB, referenced by no Dockerfile.
image-comfy/
image-models/

# Database dumps — 50 MB of real chat/session data, referenced by no Dockerfile.
embedding/

# Dependencies are installed inside the image; never ship the host's copies.
**/node_modules/

# Agent tooling and git worktrees — .claude/worktrees holds whole repo copies.
.claude/
.claude-flow/
.swarm/

# VCS metadata.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Python caches and virtualenvs.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# Frontend build outputs — regenerated inside the image.
**/.svelte-kit/
**/.next/
front_end/owui/build/

# Generated artifacts and local scratch.
graphify-out/
**/*.log
deployment.log

# Secrets must never enter a build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
